 Requires Python 3.9+; `tmux_check.py` also needs tmux. Pin runs to idle cores with `--cpus` for stable figures. See
 [docs/BENCHMARKS.md](../docs/BENCHMARKS.md) for methodology and results.
 
+## Escaping
+
+The charts are SVG documents, and some of the text in them comes from outside: labels (`--builds`, `--label`, the build names
+`environment.txt` gives) and values the results hold (a `pauses.jsonl` step name). `report.py` escapes every such value where
+it is written into the markup, text nodes and attribute values (`aria-label`) alike (`esc()`): `&`, `<`, `>`, `"` and `'`
+become entities. A label can therefore only be text: it cannot close its `<text>`, add an element or an attribute, or add a
+script, and the document parses whatever it contains. Quotation marks are escaped in text nodes too, where they would be legal
+as they are: the picture is the same, and there is no second variant to use by mistake. Each value is escaped once, at its
+insertion point, never where it is built: `&` is written as `&amp;` and never `&amp;amp;`. Unicode is written as it is, and
+the Markdown tables are not SVG: they print labels as given.
+
+`python3 bench/test_report.py` (or `python3 -m unittest discover -s bench -p "test_*.py"`) draws charts with ordinary figures,
+Unicode and malicious labels, titles and step names, and parses every document with `xml.etree.ElementTree`.
+
 ## Windows
 
 The tools run on Windows 10 2004 or later with Python from python.org (`winproc.py`): every process in a Job object of its own
